  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">High Impact Programme for the Corporate Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme aims to facilitate a transformative shift of energy-intensive industries, agribusinesses and the mining sector to a low-carbon pathway by promoting the uptake of high climate impact technologies and stimulating behavioural change at the corporate governance and management level. 

&#x2022; The programme is GCF&#x2019;s first at-scale investment to incentivize the uptake of low-carbon technologies in the industrial sector by promoting technology transfer and financing potentially process disruptive energy efficiency and low carbon investments.
&#x2022; The financing structure is tailored to overcome the initial reluctance of managements to disrupt existing industrial processes and adopt state of the art industrial technologies.
&#x2022; The programme will ultimately contribute to enhancing commercial viability of low-carbon investments by driving more corporates to commit to a potentially disruptive climate investment decisions, thereby creating economies of scale.</narrative>
  </description>
